<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">armor</ansi>

<ansi fg="command">Armor</ansi> provides damage mitigation across three channels.
Each channel has its own mitigation percentage, capped
at 75% maximum.

<ansi fg="yellow">Physical Mitigation</ansi>
  Reduces damage from melee attacks, ranged weapons, and
  physical spells. Comes from:
  - Worn equipment (plate armor, shields, helmets)
  - Natural armor (species traits, mutations)
  - Magical effects (shield spells, enchantments)

<ansi fg="yellow">Magical Mitigation</ansi>
  Reduces damage from offensive spells that target the
  mind. Comes from:
  - Enchanted equipment (robes, amulets, rings)
  - Mutation-based magical resistance

<ansi fg="yellow">Conviction Mitigation</ansi>
  Reduces conviction damage from social attacks like
  <ansi fg="command">taunt</ansi>. Comes from:
  - Willpower-themed gear (amulets, pendants)
  - Mental fortitude items

<ansi fg="yellow">Viewing Your Mitigation</ansi>
  Use <ansi fg="command">status</ansi> to see your current stats and equipment.
  Your total mitigation stacks from all equipped items.

<ansi fg="yellow">Related: </ansi>
  <ansi fg="command">help combat</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help equip</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help status</ansi>,
  <ansi fg="command">help taunt</ansi>
